  "question": {
    "text": "A very long cylindrical wire is carrying a current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;distributed uniformly over its cross-section area. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is the centre of the cross-section of the wire and the&nbsp;direction of current in into the plane of the figure. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msubsup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>.</mo><mover><mi>dI</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> along the path&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> (from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>) is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image18-79aaaebc-535a-455e-9ea2-d1e6f3a28208.jpg\" />",
